Exit 124 means it was killed (likely a runner cap or a slow/hung file), and `tail` buffered so I got no diagnostics. Let me build per-file with flushed progress so I see exactly where it stands, in two batches.

<<<RUN cwd=LeanEuclidPlus>>>
export PATH="$HOME/.venvs/leaneuclid/bin:$PATH"
for m in step1 step2 step3 step4 step5 step6 step7 step8 step9 step10 step11; do
  echo "############ building Book1.Prop45.$m";
  lake build Book1.Prop45.$m 2>&1;
  echo "---- exit=$? for $m";
done
<<<END>>>

Now let me build the fixed steps plus the remaining ones and Main.

<<<RUN cwd=LeanEuclidPlus>>>
export PATH="$HOME/.venvs/leaneuclid/bin:$PATH"
for m in step6 step8 step12 step13 step14 step15 step16 step17 step18 step19 step20 step21 Main; do
  echo "############ building Book1.Prop45.$m";
  lake build Book1.Prop45.$m 2>&1 | grep -vE "Replayed|linter can be disabled|unused variable|declaration uses 'sorry'|load-dynlib|LEAN_PATH" ;
  echo "---- exit=${PIPESTATUS[0]} for $m";
done
<<<END>>>
